{
 "author": "pk11",
 "conventions": {
  "assembly": "ratios R to Z (D4L0 E000, D4ML0 S0000) as truncated series in t = 1/J. D4L0 (theta f = f): c_e = R(E100), c_f = R(E001); L0 = sum_{a,b,k} C(2,k) (-c_e)^(2-a-b) (-c_f)^(2-k) R(Eabk) - E[X_c]^2, E[X_c] = R(E101) - c_e c_f. D4ML0: c_e = R(S1000), c_f = R(S0100); L0 = sum over the 16 subsets of R(S) times (-c) for each factor left out (c_e for e and te, c_f for f and tf) - E[X_c]^2, E[X_c] = R(S1100) - c_e c_f",
  "factor_p": "['p', c]: the vacres K3 polynomial on column c ('p', (3c, 3c+1, 3c+2), q1, q2, q3): the trial vacuum on both outer columns",
  "factor_xi": "['xi', [u, v]]: ('xi', (u, v, v), 0.0, e_1)",
  "graph": "kt_s8h_mk's window: lapl2.strip_graph columns with vacmod2's A_EX, B_EX ends (a vac column keeps its (3c, 3c+2) edge), vertex 3 c + r, row r = 0 the top, pairs as listed (F = V + #pairs)",
  "packing": "the kernel largest code D (D+1)^(F-1) against 2^63 - 1 (int64) and 2^64 - 1 (uint64)",
  "trick": "both outer columns carry the trial vacuum p, so these ratios carry route 0 (b)'s eigen-trick condition (a), settled with pk02's l0 block",
  "use": "q_L0 = sqrt(L0) bounds ||Q0 X u|| at every plane at or beyond the window's left outer column, S8's half-step LH plane among them (DESIGN_P2_12_v1_4 sect. 3.1). R6.5 reads q_L0,hi per piece: L0's upper end over the piece's t-box [1/J_hi, 1/J_lo]."
 },
